+Windows/iOS: do a Mono backpatch store that misses the RW alias outside the code invalidation lock
+
+MonoBackpatcherWrite write-owns CodeInvalidationMutex for its store. On iOS
+a store whose RW alias lookup misses goes to the guest's R+X page and
+faults; the ARM64EC access-violation handler then takes
+ThreadCreationMutex. So this thread waits for ThreadCreationMutex while
+holding CodeInvalidationMutex, the reverse of every other path
+(BTCpu64NotifyReadFile, NotifyUnmapViewOfSection, the write-fault path),
+and two threads wait on each other forever.
+
+Seen on 64-bit Unity games stuck loading (Test 12/13 Get Help logs, Nov 13
+2026: Silksong, ULTRAKILL, Cult of the Lamb, Boomerang Fu, PvZ RH, Body
+Pay): "[fexlock] STUCK" on CodeInvalidationMutex with the owner at
+MonoBackpatcherWrite (xtajit64.dll RVA 0x2044c) against
+"RtlpWaitForCriticalSection ... wait timed out" on GetThreadCreationMutex
+(RVA 0x42d858), held by a worker in BTCpu64NotifyReadFile /
+HandleImageUnmap.
+
+On a miss the store now runs after the lock scope ends, as an ordinary
+guest SMC write. A hit still stores to the writable alias under the lock.
+InvalidateGuestCodeRange is unchanged. Off: MADEIRA_MONO_MISS_UNLOCKED=0.
+
+Applies on FEX a77d5687 after 0001, 0002 and 0003 (they do not touch
+Core.cpp). Madeira-only: not for FEX-Emu.
+
