+/* patch 0124 (opt-in with 0105's switch): serve the allocator object's own asks inside ITS bounds.
+ * 0123's log: the object that rejects every grant (V8's sandbox allocator) has start 0x7000000000, size 1 TB and a 32 GB reserved prefix (+0x30 = 0x800000000). It picks random hints in
+ * [start + 32 GB, start + 1 TB) = [0x7800000000, 0x17000000000), asks the page allocator for 8/4/2/1 GB aligned to the size, and frees anything below start + 32 GB or above the end.
+ * iOS has no address above 0x8000000000, so the only place that qualifies is the top 32 GB (0x7800000000..0x8000000000), the idle real view PartitionAlloc's two pools sit in
+ * (they only use the first MB of each half). Serve a power-of-two ask of 1..8 GB with a hint in that band from the top of that view, aligned to its size. */
